   "id": "04_C4_C4b_C4c-006",
   "finding": "report #24 (ionization ratio k; symbol scheme)",
   "old": "The InP multiplier's ionization-coefficient ratio (the ratio of hole to electron impact-ionization rates) is $k\\approx0.4$–0.5 (vs about 0.02 for Si).",
   "new": "The InP multiplier's ionization-coefficient ratio $k$, the impact-ionization coefficient of the weaker-ionizing carrier divided by that of the stronger one (electron/hole in InP, where holes ionize more readily; hole/electron in Si), is $k\\approx0.4$–0.5, against about 0.02 for Si.",
   "why": "In InP hole/electron is about 2-2.5; the 0.4-0.5 figure is electron/hole. Definition per the symbol scheme."
