   "id": "04_C4_C4b_C4c-007",
   "finding": "report #39 (in §C4 item 2)",
   "old": "In sunlight they would run ≈700× over their count-rate ceiling, the highest rate they can sustain with the long hold-off (a deliberately extended dead time) that afterpulsing forces (§C4c) [I/E].",
   "new": "In sunlight they would exceed their count-rate ceiling, the highest rate they can sustain with the hold-off (a deliberately extended dead time) that afterpulsing forces, by ≈700× with a 1 µs hold-off and by ≈7,000× with the 10 µs that keeps afterpulsing below 3% (§C4c subsection 3) [I/E].",
   "why": "700x holds for a 1 us hold-off that still leaves ~8% afterpulsing; <3% needs 10 us (Telesca table)."
