   "id": "04_C4_C4b_C4c-015",
   "finding": "report #7; follow-up consistency flag (Luminar/MicroVision)",
   "old": "**Where 1,550 nm ToF survives.** Pulsed time-of-flight (ToF) lidar at 1,550 nm survives where long range is worth its price: at NIO (Seyond Falcon K3, 450 m at 10%), in trucks and off-road vehicles, in defence and very long range (AEye; MicroVision ex-Luminar), and as the natural band for FMCW (frequency-modulated continuous-wave, coherent) lidar.",
   "new": "**Where 1,550 nm survives.** Pulsed time-of-flight (ToF) lidar at 1,550 nm survives where long range is worth its price: at NIO (Seyond Falcon K3, 450 m at 10%, §C3), in trucks and off-road vehicles, and in defence and very long range (AEye; MicroVision, which bought Luminar's lidar business, §C3a). Separately, 1,550 nm is the natural band for FMCW (frequency-modulated continuous-wave, coherent) lidar (§C4c subsection 6).",
   "why": "FMCW is not ToF; replace the telegraphic 'ex-Luminar'; point the K3 range to §C3."
