  {
   "id": "04_C4_C4b_C4c-016",
   "finding": "report polish (3302 dead time used before defined; V_bd and V_ex unused)",
   "old": "A **SPAD** (single-photon avalanche diode) is a Geiger-mode avalanche photodiode biased above breakdown ($V_{\\rm bd}$, the breakdown voltage) by an excess bias $V_{\\rm ex}$ (volts above $V_{\\rm bd}$). \"Geiger mode\" means that each detected photon triggers a binary avalanche, a full-size pulse whatever the number of photons that caused it, which must be quenched (stopped) and the cell recharged. During that dead time $\\tau_d$ (a few to tens of ns) the cell is blind.",
   "new": "A **SPAD** (single-photon avalanche diode) is a Geiger-mode avalanche photodiode biased above its breakdown voltage by an excess bias. \"Geiger mode\" means that each detected photon triggers a binary avalanche, a full-size pulse whatever the number of photons that caused it, which must be quenched (stopped) and the cell recharged. The interval from an avalanche until the cell can fire again is its dead time $\\tau_d$ (a few to tens of ns), during which the cell is blind.",
   "why": "Define dead time before using it; V_bd and V_ex are not used in this section (§C6(f) defines its own)."
  },
  {
