   "id": "04_C4_C4b_C4c-049",
   "finding": "report polish (3504: Lambertian)",
   "old": "it scatters the incident sunlight equally into all directions of the hemisphere, so its photon radiance",
   "new": "it scatters the incident sunlight with the same radiance in every direction of the hemisphere (its intensity falls as the cosine of the angle from the surface normal), so its photon radiance",
   "why": "Lambertian means equal radiance, not equal intensity."
  },
  {
   "id": "04_C4_C4b_C4c-050",
   "finding": "consistency flag (Eq. (67) duplicates Eq. (24) and Eq. (81))",
   "old": "Atmospheric loss between scene and sensor is neglected (clear air, short range).",
   "new": "Atmospheric loss between scene and sensor is neglected (clear air, short range). Eq. (67) is the per-pixel model of Eq. (24) (§C0 subsection 5) and Eq. (81) (§C6(d)), written with the photon flux $\\Phi$ in place of $E_\\odot/E_{\\rm ph}$ and $\\eta_{\\rm det}$ in place of PDE.",
   "why": "Cross-reference the duplicated background-rate equation."
