   "old": "processed InP is about 1.4–3.4 orders of magnitude (24× to 2,400×) dearer than 28 nm silicon, depending on volume (derived below).",
   "new": "processed InP is about 1.4–3.4 orders of magnitude (24× to 2,400×) dearer than 28 nm silicon, depending on volume (derived below). Against the ≈\\$0.1 per mm² of a stacked Sony SPAD die (§C5a), processed InP at 1–10 €/mm² costs 10–100× as much, the figure used in subsection 6.",
